      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a generated file https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/bazel/rbe/README.md\n\nIt corresponds to the clang-11 that is installed on the Docker container that we use to run our remote Bazel Builds. \nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/bazel/rbe/gce_linux_container/Dockerfile\nNow, that version of clang is only used to compile some Bazel host tools - when we compile Skia, we use our hermetic toolchain which is controlled by toolchain/linux_amd64_toolchain_config.bzl, which you\u0027ve updated to always be C++20",
